  "pvTitle": "Consent & your rights",
  "pvSubtitle": "What TriIQ stores, who sees it, and your choices",
  "pvIntro": "TriIQ has no account, no server and no tracking. Your data stays on this device and goes only to the services you connect yourself.",
  "pvDataTitle": "What is processed",
  "pvDataBody": "• Activities and routes (GPS tracks) from Intervals.icu\n• Health and wellness data: heart rate, HRV, resting heart rate, sleep, weight and how you feel. This is health data, a special category under the GDPR.\n• Your profile: name, picture, thresholds, goals and plans\n• API keys for the services you connect",
  "pvStoredTitle": "Where it is stored",
  "pvStoredBody": "Only on this device: a local database and app preferences. API keys are kept in the operating system's secure storage. Android's cloud backup is switched off for the app. TriIQ has no server and receives none of your data.",
  "pvRecipientsTitle": "Who receives data",
  "pvRecipientsBody": "• Intervals.icu: your training data is synced with your account, using your API key.\n• Your AI provider (Claude by Anthropic, Ollama Cloud, or your own Ollama server): only when you have allowed it below and use the AI trainer, Train now, the weekly note or AI-written plan content. The conversation and the training and health data it needs are sent.\n• OpenStreetMap tile servers: only when a route map is shown. They see your IP address and the map area.\nNothing else: no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising.",
  "pvTransferTitle": "Transfers outside the EU/EEA",
  "pvTransferBody": "Some of these services may process data outside the EU/EEA (for example an AI provider in the USA). Their own privacy terms apply to what they receive. A self-hosted Ollama server on your own network keeps the data with you.",
  "pvBasisTitle": "Legal basis",
  "pvBasisBody": "Syncing with Intervals.icu happens because you connected your account. Sending health and training data to an AI provider happens only with your explicit consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) and 9(2)(a)), which you can withdraw at any time below. Map tiles are fetched only to show the map you opened; you can switch that off.",
  "pvRetentionTitle": "How long",
  "pvRetentionBody": "Until you delete it: data stays on your device until you erase it here, restore a backup over it or uninstall the app. Data already sent to Intervals.icu or an AI provider is kept by them under their own rules.",
  "pvRightsTitle": "Your rights",
  "pvRightsBody": "• Access and portability: Settings → Data & privacy → Backup exports everything stored here as one file.\n• Rectification: correct your data in Intervals.icu; the next sync updates this device.\n• Erasure: use \"Delete all data\" below. To remove your data at Intervals.icu or an AI provider, use their account tools.\n• Withdraw consent or object: switch the AI off below, or disconnect Intervals.icu in Profile.\n• Complaint: you can complain to your data protection authority.",
  "pvControlsTitle": "Your choices",
  "pvAiConsentTitle": "Send my data to the AI provider",
  "pvAiConsentHelp": "Allows training and health data to be sent to your AI provider when you use the AI trainer. Off: the AI features stay unavailable.",
  "pvAiConsentSince": "Allowed on {date}",
  "@pvAiConsentSince": {"placeholders": {"date": {"type": "String"}}},
  "pvMapTilesTitle": "Load map tiles from OpenStreetMap",
  "pvMapTilesHelp": "Route maps need tiles from OpenStreetMap, which sees your IP address and the area shown. Off: routes are drawn without a map.",
  "pvEraseTitle": "Delete all data on this device",
  "pvEraseHelp": "Removes activities, wellness, plans, settings, saved keys and the offline queue from this device and disconnects Intervals.icu. It does not delete anything at Intervals.icu or your AI provider.",
  "pvEraseButton": "Delete all data…",
  "pvEraseConfirmTitle": "Delete all data?",
  "pvEraseConfirmBody": "Everything TriIQ stores on this device will be removed and the app disconnected. Export a backup first if you want to keep it. This cannot be undone.",
